# META_HARNESS.omt — OMT-HDL v1 single source of truth (meta_harness_dsl R8).
# GUID:META_HARNESS | VERSION:3.0 | FOR:opencode-plugins + llm-agent
#
# Consumers: the opencode plugins (via .meta/.omt/harness.ir.json) and the LLM
# agent (via the GENERATED AGENTS.md projection + omt_nav index answers).
# NEVER hand-edit projections: AGENTS.md, opencode.jsonc harnessc blocks,
# .meta/.omt/harness.ir.json, .meta/.omt/nav.index.jsonl.
# Workflow: edit THIS file → uv run scripts/omt/harnessc.py check → build.
# Grammar: @kind id k=v k="v v" : payload   (# comments; refs = @kind.id; {@var.x} interpolates vars in payloads/attrs — OPT-C)

@version omt_hdl n=1

# ============================================================
# VAR — single-sourced constants (audit P1; F2/F17 root is ctx-derived)
# ============================================================
@var unlock_window_ms : 28800000
@var ledger_cap_bytes : 65536
@var ledger_path : .meta/.omt/ledger.jsonl
@var thoughts_path : .meta/.omt/thoughts.jsonl
@var receipt_path : .meta/.omt/omt_harness_e2e_last_run.json
@var ir_path : .meta/.omt/harness.ir.json
@var nav_index_path : .meta/.omt/nav.index.jsonl
@var e2e_test : tests/scripts/omt/test_omt_harness_e2e.py
@var e2e_cmd : uv run pytest tests/scripts/omt/test_omt_harness_e2e.py -q
@var thought_pattern : ^\s*(#|//|/\*|<!--|--)\s*TA:
@var doc_paths : .meta/,AGENTS.md,WORK.md
@var process_root : .meta/software_development_process
@var design_features : .meta/software_development_process/4.design/features
@var plugin_dir : .opencode/plugins/
@var enforcer_lib : .opencode/lib/enforcer/
@var shared_lib : .opencode/lib/omt_shared.ts
@var mvc_check : uv run scripts/omt/mvc_check.py
@var tdd_check : uv run scripts/omt/tdd_check.py
@var scaffold : uv run scripts/omt/new_feature.py
@var harnessc : uv run scripts/omt/harnessc.py
@var edit_tools : edit|write|patch|multiedit
@var search_tools : grep|glob|rg|find
@var harness_paths : AGENTS.md,opencode.jsonc,.meta/META_HARNESS.omt,.meta/software_development_process/omt_agent_guide.md,.opencode/plugins/omt_,.opencode/lib/omt_,.opencode/lib/enforcer/,scripts/omt/,.meta/templates/,.meta/software_development_process/2.requirements/features/feature_006.opencode_process_enforcement/,tests/scripts/omt/
@var net_paths : src/,tests/,.opencode/,scripts/omt/
@var root_allowlist : AGENTS.md,LICENSE,README.md,WORK.md,WORK_ARCHIVE.md,opencode.jsonc,pyproject.toml,uv.lock,.gitignore,.python-version,.meta,.opencode,.agents,.agents_prompts,prompts,scripts,shared,src,tests,tests_automated,tools,.projects,.workflows,sandbox
@var projects_root : .projects/meta
@var projects_archive : .projects/archive
@var project_resume_threshold_bytes : 16384
@var work_done_max : 10
# F1 (feature_052.opencode_version_canary): audited live-binary line — session start warns + canary suite fails when `opencode --version` falls outside; re-baseline deliberately (live smoke + full suite on the new binary, then bump here + rebuild)
@var opencode_version_range : >=1.18.29,<1.19

# ============================================================
# DENY — NEVER command rules (→ opencode.jsonc generated blocks)
# ============================================================
@deny bash.git_commit scope=bash match="git commit *" msg=@msg.deny_git : NEVER commit without explicit user request (Core Directive #1)
@deny bash.git_push scope=bash match="git push *" msg=@msg.deny_git : NEVER push without explicit user request
@deny bash.python scope=bash match="python *" msg=@msg.deny_uv : Python runs through uv only
@deny bash.python3 scope=bash match="python3 *" msg=@msg.deny_uv : Python runs through uv only
@deny bash.pip scope=bash match="pip *" msg=@msg.deny_uv : pip via uv only
@deny bash.pip3 scope=bash match="pip3 *" msg=@msg.deny_uv : pip via uv only
@deny bash.pytest scope=bash match="pytest *" msg=@msg.deny_uv : pytest via uv run only
@deny read.env scope=read match="*.env" msg=@msg.deny_env : .env reads denied
@deny read.env_star scope=read match="*.env.*" msg=@msg.deny_env : .env.* reads denied
@deny net.webfetch scope=toplevel match="webfetch" msg=@msg.deny_webfetch : webfetch denied

# ============================================================
# PROTECT — NEVER path rules (receipt_guard.isProtected)
# ============================================================
@protect core.env path=".env" hard=true msg=@msg.protect_env : .env never editable — no override exists
@protect core.env_dot path=".env.*" hard=true msg=@msg.protect_env : .env.* never editable — no override exists
@protect core.readme path="README.md" hard=false msg=@msg.protect_file : editable ONLY under omt_skip{scope:all} (AGENTS.md #5: unless explicitly asked)
@protect core.uvlock path="uv.lock" hard=false msg=@msg.protect_file : editable ONLY under omt_skip{scope:all}
@protect core.license path="LICENSE" hard=false msg=@msg.protect_file : editable ONLY under omt_skip{scope:all}

# ============================================================
# ALWAYS — standing rules
# ============================================================
@always git_status run="git status" : run git log/status before and during work
@always meta_md glob="META.md" : consult META.md per directory on demand
@always phase_first run="omt_phase" : omt_phase{task_type,phase,scope} before any src/ edit
@always artifacts run="omt_complete" : produce phase artifacts per the §12 matrix
@always tests_green run="uv run pytest" : tests must pass before phase completion

# ============================================================
# PHASE — §12 artifact matrix + lifecycle FSM
# ============================================================
@phase decl_only applies="bug_fix,minor_feature,refactor,test" requires="decl" : phase declaration only
@phase design_req applies="major_feature,new_screen" requires="decl,design" : phase + design doc on disk (auto-detected under 4.design/features/feature_<n>/ or design_doc= arg)
@phase docs_none applies="docs" requires="none" : no phase required
@fsm phase states="Analysis,Design,Programming,Testing,Done" initial="Analysis" transitions="Analysis>Design,Testing;Design>Programming,Analysis;Programming>Testing,Design,Analysis;Testing>Analysis,Design,Programming,Done" : OMT++ phase lifecycle (guide §12)

# ============================================================
# TDD — two-hats state machine (feature_016)
# ============================================================
@fsm tdd states="TESTLIST,RED,GREEN,REFACTOR,DONE" initial="TESTLIST" auto_on="major_feature@Programming,new_screen@Programming" : TDD cycle omt_testlist → omt_red → omt_green → omt_refactor → omt_done
@hat tdd.testlist allow="" : no edits — behavior list (JSON array canonical; prose auto-split)
@hat tdd.red allow="tests/" revert_on="" : tests/ edits ALLOWED, src/ BLOCKED (fail verified true-RED: imports target, fails on missing behavior)
@hat tdd.green allow="src/" revert_on="" : tests/ BLOCKED, src/ ALLOWED (pass verified)
@hat tdd.refactor allow="src/" revert_on="tests_break" : src/ ALLOWED, auto-revert if tests break
@hat tdd.done allow="" : validation only (full suite + coverage gaps + dangling reds)

# ============================================================
# PRED — closed gate-condition vocabulary (HDL-1: data only; TS owns builtins)
# ============================================================
@pred path_in : path_in(glob|@var) — repo-relative path matches glob/prefix set
@pred cmd_match : cmd_match(@deny.*) — bash command matches a deny pattern
@pred ledger_has : ledger_has(kind,k=v,window) — ledger record of kind within window ms
@pred session_flag : session_flag(name) | !session_flag(name) — per-session container flag
@pred file_has : file_has("lit") — target file content carries literal
@pred receipt_fresh : receipt_fresh() — e2e receipt timestamp >= target mtime
@pred fsm_allows : fsm_allows(@fsm.tdd,path) — current TDD hat allows the path
@pred risk_high : risk_high() — target file carries a TA: risk: thought (drops cross-session window)
@pred net_marking : net_marking(active>1) — live concurrency probe (wraps omt_net{op:probe} marking); true when 2+ works active (work_active>1 or 2+ f{N}_active holders); solo → g.net skips, phase-gate only (feature_053 C1)

# ============================================================
# GATE — the enforcer concerns as data (guard order pinned; LOGIC stays TS in HDL-1)
# ============================================================
@gate g.nav on=before tools="grep|glob|rg|find" paths=@var.doc_paths when=path_in(@var.doc_paths) requires=session_flag(nav_used) msg=@msg.nav_required hard=true skip_ok=true order=0 : nav tools before doc searches (feature_020); read + src/non-doc exempt; C2: bug_fix/test phase auto-satisfies
@gate g.protect on=before tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(@protect.*) msg=@msg.protect_file hard=true skip_ok=true order=10 : NEVER paths; .env* hard (no skip), README/uv.lock/LICENSE via scope=all
@gate g.receipt on=before tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(@var.harness_paths) requires=receipt_fresh() msg=@msg.receipt_stale hard=true skip_ok=false order=20 : second-edit guard on the harness surface (git-dirty + mtime vs receipt)
@gate g.tests on=before tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(tests/) requires=ledger_has(skip,tests_approved=true,@var.unlock_window_ms) msg=@msg.tests_canary hard=true skip_ok=true order=30 : canary approval; TDD hat decides when tdd_mode active; C2: own test dir auto-approved in RED
@gate g.net on=before tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(@var.net_paths) msg=@msg.net_required hard=true skip_ok=false order=35 : net permission-to-act (feature_050 Alt A; feature_053 C1: engages only when net_marking(active>1) — solo sessions skip to phase-gate only, impl-owned check); calls omt_net{op:gate} — fail-closed unless omt_skip{scope:"all"} expiry+audit
@gate g.phase on=before tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(src/) requires=ledger_has(phase|skip) msg=@msg.no_phase hard=true skip_ok=true order=40 : declared phase; design artifact also required for major_feature/new_screen
@gate g.think on=before tools=@var.edit_tools when=file_has("TA:") requires=ledger_has(think_consult) msg=@msg.think_gate hard=true skip_ok=false order=50 : consult via omt_think{op:list,path} — NOT skip-bypassable; risk: thoughts drop the cross-session window
@gate g.tdd_after on=after tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(src/) requires=fsm_allows(@fsm.tdd,path) msg=@msg.tdd_revert hard=false skip_ok=false order=70 : REFACTOR auto-revert when tests break + advisories
@gate g.mvc on=after tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(src/**/*.py) run=@var.mvc_check msg=@msg.mvc_new_hard hard=true skip_ok=false order=60 : block NEWLY introduced hard MVC++ violations (delta vs pre-edit snapshot; correct-forward)
@gate g.kb on=before tools=@var.edit_tools when=path_in(src/) requires=session_flag(kb_consulted) msg=@msg.kb_required hard=true skip_ok=false order=55 : KB consult — src/ edits need prior omt_kb_nav consult (feature_kb_akb); C2: bug_fix/test phase auto-satisfies

# ============================================================
# MSG — block/warn text (ERR_/WRN_ + enforcer literals; TS renders in HDL-1)
# ============================================================
@msg deny_git sev=block see=@doc.rule.r1 : git commit/push is NEVER without an explicit user request (Core Directive #1)
@msg deny_uv sev=block : Python must run through uv — never bare python/pip/pytest
@msg deny_env sev=block : .env files are denied (secrets)
@msg deny_webfetch sev=block : webfetch is denied in this repo
@msg protect_env sev=block : '{rel}' is protected (.env / secrets) — NEVER editable, no override (Core Directives #2)
@msg protect_file sev=block : '{rel}' is protected (README.md / uv.lock / LICENSE). Edit refused; if truly intended ask the user, then omt_skip{scope:"all"}
@msg tests_canary sev=block : editing '{rel}' requires explicit canary-test approval (Stop Point #4). Unlock: omt_skip{reason:"approved canary test", scope:"tests"}
@msg net_required sev=block : net permission denied for '{rel}' — fire(work_start) required, stale-rev/drift/conflicts block (feature_050); break-glass: omt_skip{scope:"all",reason:"..."} (expiring, audited)
@msg no_phase sev=block see=@doc.rule.r1 : declare your OMT++ phase before editing src/ ('{rel}'): omt_phase{task_type, scope}. Trivial fix? task_type:"bug_fix" is enough. Override: omt_skip{reason:"..."}
@msg artifact sev=block see=@doc.rule.r2 : task_type '{tt}' may not edit src/ until a design artifact exists (guide §12); auto-detected under 4.design/features/ from the feature slug ('{feature}'), or design_doc=; scaffold: {@var.scaffold} "<name>" --type {tt}
@msg nav_required sev=block see=@doc.nav.enforcement : before grep/glob on META HARNESS docs use omt_nav (op=nav|list_sections|cross_ref|quick_ref) first; read and src/non-doc searches exempt; override omt_skip{scope:"nav"}; examples: omt_nav{op:"nav", query:"SECTION:"} · omt_nav{op:"list_sections"} · omt_nav{op:"quick_ref", workflow:"..."}
@msg think_gate sev=block see=@doc.think.gate : '{rel}' carries TA: thoughts — review the listed thoughts, then clear with omt_think{op:"list", path:"{rel}"} (the call records the consult)
@msg receipt_stale sev=block : '{rel}' is part of the META HARNESS surface and already has unverified changes — run the harness e2e before editing again: {@var.e2e_cmd} (refreshes {@var.receipt_path})
@msg mvc_new_hard sev=block see=@msg.err_v2m : your edit introduced a hard MVC++ violation in {rel} (guide §16) — fix it forward now
@msg tdd_revert sev=block : REFACTOR broke tests — edit reverted
@msg mvc_warn sev=warn : MVC++ advisory warnings on {rel} — run {@var.mvc_check} {rel}
@msg err_v2m sev=block : View imports Model (ui/ ← model.*) — BLOCK
@msg err_m2v sev=block : Model imports View/UI (model/ ← ui.*) — BLOCK
@msg err_prt_abc sev=block : Abstract Partner not ABC+abstractmethod — BLOCK
@msg wrn_sql_dp sev=warn : SQL outside DP classes (non-*_db.py has SQL) — TOAST
@msg wrn_god_ctl sev=warn : Controller >300 lines — TOAST
@msg wrn_ctl_ui sev=warn : print()/console in Controller — TOAST
@msg wrn_opencode_version sev=warn : opencode binary {rel} is outside the audited range ({@var.opencode_version_range}) — gates were audited against that line; re-run the live canary suite and re-baseline the range before trusting gate behavior
@msg kb_required sev=block : KB consult required — run omt_kb_nav{op:nav, query} (tag-prefix CLASS_/CONTRACT_/DEP_/LAYER_ or symbol id; tag_type:TIER_CODE) before editing src/ (feature_kb_akb)

# ============================================================
# STATE — runtime state files (mode: append|rotate|rewrite)
# ============================================================
@state ledger path=@var.ledger_path mode=rotate cap=@var.ledger_cap_bytes window=@var.unlock_window_ms truth="ledger.jsonl hot + latest ledger-YYYYMM.jsonl archive" : audit log {ts,kind:phase|skip|complete|think_consult,...}; 8h unlock window
@state thoughts path=@var.thoughts_path mode=append truth="grep TA:" : append-only sidecar (add/verify/remove-tombstone; latest-wins fold; verdicts join on normalized text F28); inline TA: is the source of truth — the index is NEVER rewritten (R6 S1)
@state receipt path=@var.receipt_path mode=rewrite truth="json passed_at + mtime" : harness e2e receipt; refreshed by @var.e2e_cmd

# ============================================================
# INJECT — conversation-resident injections (ONE per trigger — R6 S6; budgets = the F32 ×N-turn control knob)
# ============================================================
@inject session_bootstrap on=first_tool_result budget=1536 : ONE emission per session (nav tip ≤512B deferred when nav-first R7 T3; compact TA digest ≤1024B DIGEST_CAP_BYTES — counts + per-file counts + stale ⚠️ + pointer, full texts via omt_think{op:list} / D1)
@inject file_thoughts on=file_read budget=1024 : first read of a TA:-carrying file per session appends the file's thoughts (feature_022 D1 point-of-use; awareness ≠ consult — no think_consult record)
@inject kb_bootstrap on=first_tool_result budget=256 : AKB tip — omt_kb_nav{op:nav, query} before src/ edits (g.kb blocks); CLASS_/CONTRACT_/DEP_/LAYER_ tags, tag_type:TIER_CODE, list_sections file:<substr> (feature_kb_akb)

# ============================================================
# DOC — harness knowledge corpus (nav-indexed; app-doc tags are scraped at build)
# ============================================================
@doc startup tags="STARTUP" : Read `WORK.md` (only) at session start; summarize current state in ≤ 15 lines (in-progress / blocked / next). Present the Tasks menu (NEXT/Other/Blocked/Resources) in order; no invented options (D19). All other docs on demand via `omt_nav` (op=nav|list_sections|cross_ref|quick_ref).
@doc runtime tags="RUNTIME" : `uv` only (no bare `python`/`pip`/`pytest`). `src/` edits → `omt_phase` first.
@doc enforcement tags="ENF" : mechanical via .opencode/plugins/omt_enforcer.ts + lib/enforcer ×7 + opencode.jsonc; reference = .meta/META_HARNESS.omt (query: omt_nav)
@doc rule.r1 tags="RULE_R1" : src/ edit REQUIRES omt_phase{task_type,phase,scope} — task_type: bug_fix|minor_feature|major_feature|new_screen|refactor|test|docs; phase: Analysis|Design|Programming|Testing; scope: one-sentence done definition
@doc rule.r2 tags="RULE_R2" : major_feature|new_screen REQUIRES design_*.md on disk — scaffold: uv run scripts/omt/new_feature.py "<name>" --type major_feature|new_screen
@doc rule.r3 tags="RULE_R3" : TDD AUTO-ACTIVATES for major_feature|new_screen in Programming — omt_tdd op=testlist→red→green→refactor→done
@doc tdd.bootstrap tags="TDD_BOOTSTRAP" : TESTLIST blocks tests/ creation (the gate precedes the first RED) → bootstrap new test files via omt_skip{reason:"...",scope:"tests"} — logged canary; blanket auto-unlock REJECTED; narrowed C2 auto-unlock: declared feature own test dir while RED active only
@doc tdd.done_allowlist tags="TDD_DONE_ALLOWLIST" : feature_051/A1: omt_done tolerates ZERO suite failures — KNOWN_SUITE_FAILURES (scripts/omt/tdd/state.py) is permanently EMPTY (shape-pinned by test_ledger_rotation.py); suite green means green; regrowing it reverts the A1 decision
@doc tdd.true_red tags="TDD_TRUE_RED" : AST+pytest verify — must import target src, fail on missing behavior (not syntax)
@doc tdd.coverage tags="TDD_COVERAGE_GAPS" : public src/ methods without test calls → blocks phase exit
@doc tdd.dangling tags="TDD_DANGLING_REDS" : tests declared RED never turned GREEN → blocks phase exit
@doc comp.enf tags="COMP_ENF" : .opencode/plugins/omt_enforcer.ts — gate plugin composition root; gate logic in .opencode/lib/enforcer/ (phase_gate, tdd_hats, think_gate, nav_gate, receipt_guard, mvc_after, session_state)
@doc comp.lib tags="COMP_LIB" : .opencode/lib/omt_shared.ts — shared single source (repo-root, state paths, THOUGHT_PATTERN, ledger IO+rotation, receipt check, thinkDigest, IR loader)
@doc comp.sts tags="COMP_STS" : .opencode/plugins/omt_status.ts — omt_status tool
@doc comp.nav tags="COMP_NAV" : .opencode/plugins/omt_nav.ts — omt_nav (op=nav|list_sections|cross_ref|quick_ref; OPT-H consolidated) answering from .meta/.omt/nav.index.jsonl
@doc comp.think tags="COMP_THINK" : .opencode/plugins/omt_think.ts — omt_think (op=add|list|remove|verify|suggest; OPT-H consolidated)
@doc comp.lnt tags="COMP_LNT" : scripts/omt/mvc_check.py — MVC++ linter
@doc comp.tdd tags="COMP_TDD" : scripts/omt/tdd_check.py — TDD engine (9 subcommands; compat shim over scripts/omt/tdd/ package: state.py, ast_checks.py, gates.py, cli.py)
@doc comp.scaf tags="COMP_SCAF" : scripts/omt/new_feature.py — feature scaffolder
@doc comp.lg tags="COMP_LG" : .meta/.omt/ledger.jsonl — audit log (phase/skip/complete records)
@doc comp.rul tags="COMP_RUL" : opencode.jsonc, AGENTS.md (GENERATED) — config + system rules
@doc comp.hdl tags="COMP_HDL" : .meta/META_HARNESS.omt + scripts/omt/harnessc.py — THIS source + its compiler (projections: harness.ir.json, AGENTS.md, nav.index.jsonl, opencode.jsonc blocks, harness.report)
@doc comp.workflows tags="COMP_WORKFLOWS" : .workflows/ — operational workflow catalog (triggered procedures the agent executes on demand); root manifest .workflows/META.md is the entry point; sits ABOVE the harness (each workflow's # Rules line 1 declares follow-vs-override OMT); no runtime/parser (agent-read markdown, two-level discovery read: root META → matched subject META → matched file; mandatory approval gate)
@doc pth.workflows tags="PTH_WORKFLOWS" : .workflows/META.md — root manifest of the operational workflow catalog (entry point read on every trigger)
@doc comp.projects tags="COMP_PROJECTS" : .projects/ — per-feature design & project-planning home; non-gated (NOT in harness_paths); subject folders .projects/meta/<feature>/{PROJECT.md, CURRENT_STATE.md, supporting artifacts}; PROJECT.md = canonical single-source design doc (sess log + resume point in CURRENT_STATE.md); companion to the phase-gated design doc (@phase design_req auto-detected under 4.design/features/feature_<n>/ OR accepts design_doc= pointing here); MECHANICAL lifecycle (feature_030): uv run scripts/omt/project.py new|link|log|status|close|reopen|archive|sync|backfill — truth = ledger project/project_link records (1 project : 0..N features); manifest .projects/meta/META.md GENERATED (project.py sync); harnessc check_projects_* enforce structure/links/resume/status/manifest
@doc pth.projects tags="PTH_PROJECTS" : .projects/meta/<feature>/PROJECT.md — canonical design doc per feature (single source of truth; CURRENT_STATE.md is the session-by-session log + resume point); closed projects may move to .projects/archive/<slug>/ (project.py archive)
# DERIVED (R9/OPT-I): doc.prot.files ← @protect+g.tests · doc.esc ← @tool omt_skip+gates
@doc ext.complete tags="EXT_COMPLETE" : omt_complete{feature,advance_to:Design|Programming|Testing|Done} → verifies phase artifacts + TDD validate-exit + syncs WORK.md [x]
@doc sts.cmd tags="STS_CMD" : omt_status tool (or: uv run scripts/omt/tdd_check.py status)
@doc sts.out tags="STS_OUT" : phase, TDD state, pending items, unlock expiry, lint baseline, WORK.md next task
@doc nav.020 tags="NAV_020" : feature_020.meta_harness_navigation — mandatory doc navigation before grep/glob on docs
@doc nav.enforcement tags="NAV_ENFORCEMENT" : scoped gate in lib/enforcer/nav_gate.ts — blocks grep/glob on doc paths until nav used; read & src/non-doc exempt; omt_skip{scope:nav} escape
@doc nav.tags tags="NAV_TAGS" : SECTION:, RULE_, ERR_, WRN_, CMD_, QUICK_, XREF_, TT_, PHASE_, FEAT_ (legacy markdown tags — now compiled index records)
@doc think.021 tags="THINK_021" : feature_021.meta_harness_think_anywhere — persistent inline TA: thought-tags
@doc think.format tags="THINK_FORMAT" : <comment> TA: [<category>: ] <thought> — e.g. # TA: gotcha: mutates history
@doc think.syntax tags="THINK_SYNTAX" : .py/.toml/.sh/.yml → # | .ts/.js/.mjs/.jsonc → // | .md/.mdx → <!-- --> | .css → /* */ | .json → DENIED
@doc think.protected tags="THINK_PROTECTED" : TA: refused on .env*, README.md, uv.lock, LICENSE, .json (no comments)
@doc think.index tags="THINK_INDEX" : .meta/.omt/thoughts.jsonl — append-only sidecar {ts,path,line,category,thought}; inline TA: is truth
@doc think.gate tags="THINK_GATE" : thinkGateDecision({hasThoughts,consulted}) → block edits to TA:-carrying files until omt_think{op:list} consulted
@doc think.gate_not_skip tags="THINK_GATE_NOT_SKIP" : think-gate NOT bypassable by omt_skip (safety-relevant); only omt_think{op:list} clears it
@doc think.digest tags="THINK_DIGEST" : first tool result of each session carries the compact TA: digest (counts + per-file counts + stale ⚠️ + pointer — R6 S7; live path tool.execute.after)
@doc think.consult tags="THINK_CONSULT" : omt_think{op:list} writes {kind:"think_consult"} to ledger → clears think-gate (feature_022 C2 per-file)
@doc pth.guide tags="PTH_GUIDE" : .meta/software_development_process/omt_agent_guide.md
@doc pth.design tags="PTH_DESIGN" : .meta/software_development_process/4.design/features/feature_XXX/
@doc pth.test tags="PTH_TEST" : .meta/software_development_process/6.testing/features/feature_XXX/
@doc pth.work tags="PTH_WORK" : WORK.md
@doc pth.rules tags="PTH_RULES" : AGENTS.md (GENERATED from .meta/META_HARNESS.omt)
@doc workflows tags="WORKFLOWS" : .workflows/ operational workflow catalog — triggered procedures the agent loads on demand (markdown recipes, NOT a runtime). Sits ABOVE the harness: each workflow's `# Rules` line 1 declares follow-vs-override OMT. Two-level discovery read: .workflows/META.md → matched subject META → matched file. Mandatory approval gate (no auto-fix). Detail: @doc comp.workflows + .workflows/META.md.
@doc projects_home tags="PROJECTS_HOME" : .projects/ per-feature design & project home — non-gated; PROJECT.md (canonical) + CURRENT_STATE.md (session log); companion to @phase design_doc. Lifecycle CLI: uv run scripts/omt/project.py (new|link|close|sync); manifest .projects/meta/META.md (GENERATED); WORK.md `## Projects` (synced). Detail: @doc comp.projects + .projects/meta/.

# DERIVED (R9/OPT-I): doc.tree.{src,tst,doc} ← @gate when= path_in chains + @phase
# ============================================================
# GOTCHA — costly re-discoveries, nav-indexed (improvement002/OPT-B;
# relocated from the WORK.md scratchpad — query: omt_nav "GOTCHA_")
# ============================================================
@doc gotcha.loader_exports tags="GOTCHA_LOADER_EXPORTS" : opencode plugin loader requires ALL named exports of a plugin .ts be functions (tool objects aren't) → plugins export ONLY `export default async () => ({tool:{...}})`; guard test pins omt_think only.
@doc gotcha.done_reachable tags="GOTCHA_DONE_REACHABLE" : omt_tdd{op:done} reachable post-R4 (opencode_live excluded; allowlist permanently empty since feature_051/A1 — any failure blocks); default phase exit stays omt_complete{advance_to:Testing→Done}.
@doc gotcha.think_gated tags="GOTCHA_THINK_GATED" : omt_think.ts + lib/enforcer/think_gate.ts are THINK-GATED (carry TA: thoughts) — omt_think{op:list,path:...} before editing clears the gate; NOT skip-bypassable.
@doc gotcha.testlist_json tags="GOTCHA_TESTLIST_JSON" : omt_tdd{op:testlist} behaviors: JSON array is canonical; newline/bullet prose is auto-split by tdd/cli.py _parse_behaviors — no re-format required.
@doc gotcha.sdk_contract tags="GOTCHA_SDK_CONTRACT" : tool.execute.after has args on input, NOT output (output={title,output,metadata} only); the BEFORE hook is the OPPOSITE (args on output) — applying the after-fix to both silently kills all before-hook guards; pinned by test_omt_enforcer_guard_source_pins.py.
@doc gotcha.live_binary tags="GOTCHA_LIVE_BINARY" : runner fixtures can't catch contract/path drift — only real-binary tests: `opencode run --format json "<prompt>"` + jq tool_use events (--pure = A/B control); assert FILE-STATE byte-identical, snapshot+restore probes; opencode loads .opencode/plugins/*.ts directly (dist/ unused).
@doc gotcha.receipt_second_edit tags="GOTCHA_RECEIPT_SECOND_EDIT" : e2e receipt guard = SECOND-EDIT guard (git-dirty + mtime vs receipt) — first edit of a CLEAN harness file allowed BY DESIGN; each edit bumps mtime > receipt → next edit of THAT file blocked until e2e rerun.
@doc gotcha.bugb_recipe tags="GOTCHA_BUGB_RECIPE" : BUG-B live test (git-dirty-first): touch/os.utime on a CLEAN file never engages the receipt guard (content-git-status-based) — probe: snapshot bytes → write_bytes(probe) (content-dirty ⇒ stale receipt) → opencode run one edit (forbid skip/bash/git) → assert bytes unchanged → restore in finally.
@doc gotcha.plugin_probe tags="GOTCHA_PLUGIN_PROBE" : plugin probes w/o live suite (R6 recipe): bun /tmp/probe.ts + await import(abs .opencode/plugins/omt_<x>.ts) + await m.default() → real tool map/hooks; imports resolve from .opencode/node_modules regardless of cwd (run from repo root); syntax gate: cd .opencode && bun build --target=bun --outfile=/dev/null plugins/<f>.ts.
@doc gotcha.write_large tags="GOTCHA_WRITE_LARGE" : Write-tool full-file writes of ~750-line guarded plugins abort with empty params → rm file (receipt guard ok on non-existent), rebuild via sequential cat >> quoted-heredoc ~100-line chunks, ONE receipt refresh at the end.
@doc gotcha.receipt_round_robin tags="GOTCHA_RECEIPT_ROUND_ROBIN" : multi-file guarded refactors: receipt guard is PER-FILE → ONE edit per file per round (parallel OK), ONE receipt refresh per round; the e2e test file is receipt-EXEMPT — update its source pins FIRST shape-agnostic, tighten at the end.
@doc gotcha.plugin_ctx tags="GOTCHA_PLUGIN_CTX" : plugin factory ctx = {project,client,$,directory,worktree}; repo root = worktree ?? directory; factories call initOmtShared(worktree ?? directory); shared-lib path getters are LAZY; tool() is identity → direct .execute(args,ctx) in probes hits the real function.
@doc gotcha.red_runnable tags="GOTCHA_RED_RUNNABLE" : TDD RED gate needs RUNNABLE red (exit 1); collection errors (exit 2) REJECTED → for not-yet-existing classes import symbols lazily inside the test (importlib) so failures surface as test failures, not ImportError at collection; new test files need omt_skip{scope:tests} canary (TDD_BOOTSTRAP).
@doc tdd.env_flaky_fixed tags="TDD_ENV_FLAKY_FIXED" : (root-caused by feature_051/A1 — demoted from GOTCHA) feature_016 TestTddCheckCli test_gate_no_tdd_* historically failed while ANY TDD session was live in the real 8h-window ledger; those subprocesses now run hermetically (OMT_LEDGER_PATH → tmp) and cannot see live sessions.
@doc gotcha.tdd_node tags="GOTCHA_TDD_NODE" : record red/green/refactor at the SAME test_node — red at f.py::C::t + green at f.py leaves latest=red blocking omt_tdd{op:done} (recovery: omt_tdd{op:green} at the exact red node); KNOWN_SUITE_FAILURES is shape-pinned EMPTY (test_ledger_rotation.py, feature_051/A1) — do NOT grow it; fix failures instead.
@doc gotcha.ts_no_reload tags="GOTCHA_TS_NO_RELOAD" : TS plugin edits do NOT hot-reload; gates shelling out to Python re-read it live every call → in-session gate changes go in the Python side; coverage gate scans ONLY tests/features/<feature>/ + counts abstract methods — READ gates.py/ast_checks.py/phase_gate.ts before writing make-work tests.
@doc gotcha.tests_canary_shadow tags="GOTCHA_TESTS_CANARY_SHADOW" : tests/ canary unlock (guardTestsPath) reads the LATEST phase/skip record for the session — omt_phase AFTER omt_skip{scope:tests} shadows the approval (a record without tests_approved wins) → declare the phase FIRST, then re-issue omt_skip{scope:"tests"} immediately before the tests/ edit.
@doc gotcha.tdd_toolchain tags="GOTCHA_TDD_TOOLCHAIN" : omt_tdd red|green|refactor is toolchain-aware—`.py` runs pytest, `.ts/.tsx` runs `npx vitest run <file>` from the vitest PROJECT ROOT (upward package.json-with-vitest-dep / vitest.config.* search), so polyglot features (petri_net_studio 034/035/036) get REAL two-hats enforcement instead of the old A11/B11 manual red→green workaround. Vitest runs the WHOLE file (no `-t` filter—vitest treats `-t` as regex and an unmatched name returns exit 0 = FALSE green/red). Declared RED/GREEN at the same test_node. (feature_038)

# ============================================================
# CONV — standing conventions (agent-behavior knowledge)
# ============================================================
@doc conv.work_done tags="CONV_WORK_DONE" : WORK.md completed tasks = ONE line + pointer (feature dir / git log) — narrative is paid every session startup; details live in git history + .meta/.../features/<f>/ (improvement003/OPT-M)
@doc conv.work_rotate tags="CONV_WORK_ROTATE" : WORK.md keeps pending + last 5 DONE inline; older DONE rotates to WORK_ARCHIVE.md (never auto-read, no nav index) — backstop @var work_done_max (improvement006/OPT-B)

